  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1103.11 Review of Applications",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1103.11 Review of Applications.\n\n(a) Upon receiving a complete application package as specified in Env-Wq 1103.02, the department shall review the application.\n\n(b) The department shall approve the proposed public bathing place if the department determines that the proposed public bathing place has been designed so as to comply with the applicable design standards of this chapter.\n\n(c) The department shall inform the applicant of its decision in writing. If the application is denied, the decision shall state the reason(s) for the denial.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100) #8468, eff 11-1-05; ss by #10577, eff 5-1-14 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100); ss by #13198, eff 5-1-21 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1100.html"
